            <div xml:id="d111-a10">

                <pb facs="0319" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg261"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 10.</seg></opener>
                <head>Department of State, Office of War and Marine–Section first.</head>
                <p>The President of the republic is informed by your despatch of the 24th July last,
                    enclosing Nos. 1 and 2 of the last correspondence between you and General Douay,
                    in regard to the exchange of the prisoners that were taken from the invading
                    army in the action at Santa Isabel, <pb facs="0320" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/>
                    that the business is still pending, as General Douay is awaiting the decision of
                    General Bazaine.</p>
                <p>You were directly authorized to attend to this business, because the
                    commander-in-chief of the army of the north, who was informed of it, was so far
                    off. The principles upon which the authorization of the exchange was based are
                    those observed by civilized nations, and which the government of the republic
                    has tried to follow in all its acts, in contrast to abuses committed by the
                    enemy.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty!
                            <placeName>Chihuahua</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-08-21">August 21, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MEJIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General A. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Viezca</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor and Military Commander of the State of
                            Coahuila de Zaragoza, at Saltillo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
